          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Grothendieck-Riemann-Roch theorem
            describes (the failure of) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
            of the behaviour of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} push forward
            along
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
          %p
            It says, in the formulation of (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahHirzebruch61"}> Atiyah-Hirzebruch 61
            ), that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+morphism"} flat morphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+morphism"} flat
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+scheme"} regular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-projective+varieties"} quasi-projective varieties
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+domain"} Dedekind domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} push-forward
            of some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is the push-forward of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            of the Chern-character of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+class"} Todd class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-orientation"} K-oriented
            maps.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} proper map
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi ch
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ∪
                              %mi Td
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ;
                          %mi ℚ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
